      "nets": ["Net-(U1-VCC)", "VCC"],
      "observed": "U1 pin 28 (VCC) is on net 'Net-(U1-VCC)' together with C17 pin 1, but this net is not connected to the main VCC net. The main VCC net includes U1 pins 6 (VBAT), 9 (VDD), 11 (BS1) but not pin 28.",
      "expected": "U1 pin 28 (VCC) should be connected to the main VCC net, as it is a power_in pin and the specification describes C7 (2.2 µF) connected to U4 VCC (digital-logic supply pin) to GND, implying VCC is the supply rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"28\") (pinfunction \"VCC\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"22\") (name \"Net-(U1-VCC)\") ... (node (ref \"C17\") (pin \"1\") ...) (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"28\") ...))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"24\") (name \"VCC\") ... (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"6\") ...) (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"9\") ...) (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"11\") ...))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C7 (2.2 µF) — U4 `VCC` (digital-logic supply pin) to GND"}
      ],
      "impact": "The OLED's VCC supply pin is left floating (only connected to a decoupling capacitor), so the OLED will not receive power on that pin and the display will likely not function.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U4"],
      "pins": ["U4.1"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U4-VBAT-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "U4 pin 1 (VBAT) is marked as unconnected with pintype 'power_in+no_connect'.",
      "expected": "For the STM32L476, if no backup battery is used, VBAT should be connected to VDD (or VCC) per standard practice and the datasheet recommendation.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\") (pintype \"power_in+no_connect\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The backup domain is unpowered; this may cause increased current consumption or unreliable operation of the RTC/backup registers, though main functions might still work.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a critical open connection: the OLED's VCC pin (U1.28) is not tied to the main VCC rail, leaving the display unpowered. A secondary issue is the unconnected VBAT pin on the MCU (U4.1)."
}

